## Why This Question Is Asked
This question tests understanding of three-valued propagation on monotone constraints and the ability to design minimal backtracking strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Three-valued logic with ordering T > U > F
- Edge-wise monotone constraints on a directed graph
- Fixed-point propagation with backtracking for conflict resolution

## Code Example
```javascript
function propagate(nodes, edges, init) {
  const rank = { 'T': 2, 'U': 1, 'F': 0 };
  let changed = true;
  while (changed) {
    changed = false;
    for (const [from, to] of edges) {
      if (rank[nodes[to]] < rank[nodes[from]]) {
        nodes[to] = nodes[from];
        changed = true;
      }
    }
  }
  return nodes;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about 3-valued logic inside a constrained satisfaction task and to design a targeted backtracking propagation routine, mirroring real policy/rule engines.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued semantics for ∧, ∨, ¬, and → via ¬A ∨ B
- Propagation of Unknowns to prune F-violating branches
- Backtracking with partial assignments in a small CSP

## Code Example
```javascript
// Implementation sketch for Kleene-style SATish propagation
const order = { 'F':0, 'U':1, 'T':2 };
function not(v){ return v==='T'?'F': v==='F'?'T':'U'; }
function and(a,b){ return order[a] < order[b] ? a : b; }
function or(a,b){ return order[a] > order[b] ? a : b; }
function imp(a,b){ return or(not(a), b); }
```

